01:53:59.850 --> 01:54:02.760
I do like I've put out, so my
approach, my approach is like,

01:54:02.760 --> 01:54:06.690
I've always been sort of a
low sugar, lower fat guy.

01:54:06.690 --> 01:54:09.330
I've made the mistake of
going no fat years ago

01:54:09.330 --> 01:54:10.163
and I paid for it.

01:54:10.163 --> 01:54:12.480
I was like in college and back in the day

01:54:12.480 --> 01:54:13.560
we were the same age.

01:54:13.560 --> 01:54:16.080
We read all the magazines
and that was what we had.

01:54:16.080 --> 01:54:16.980
We didn't have an internet then.

01:54:16.980 --> 01:54:18.510
So we were reading magazines

01:54:18.510 --> 01:54:21.213
and the recommended
path was to go low fat.

01:54:22.200 --> 01:54:25.620
It helps you to become
hypo caloric very easily

01:54:25.620 --> 01:54:29.280
because the density of the
calories in a gram of fat

01:54:29.280 --> 01:54:31.140
versus a gram of carbohydrates or protein

01:54:31.140 --> 01:54:34.440
is nine versus four for
the carbs and protein.

01:54:34.440 --> 01:54:37.110
So if you're cutting out
grams of fat on a daily basis,

01:54:37.110 --> 01:54:39.030
you're quickly cutting out calories

01:54:39.030 --> 01:54:40.770
that allows you to get leaner.

01:54:40.770 --> 01:54:44.100
Well, of course as everything,
I mean, if little is good,

01:54:44.100 --> 01:54:45.090
then a lot is better.

01:54:45.090 --> 01:54:48.420
So I would cut all of them
out or almost all of them

01:54:48.420 --> 01:54:53.420
and at the age of 22, 21,
I'm like standing at a stop

01:54:54.200 --> 01:54:55.740
up at University of Connecticut

01:54:55.740 --> 01:54:58.650
waiting for the tram to
come and bring me to campus.

01:54:58.650 --> 01:55:00.690
And I couldn't even open my eyes

01:55:00.690 --> 01:55:02.910
